l_2479","name":"Paul","also":"Saul, Mercurius","summary":"Saul was born about the same time as our Lord. His circumcision-name was Saul, and probably the name Paul was also given to him in infancy “for use in the Gentile world,” as “Saul” would be his Hebrew home-name.","verses":179,"father":"","mother":"","v":[1,12,13]},{"id":"sosthenes_2772","name":"Sosthenes","also":"","summary":"Safe in strength, the chief ruler of the synagogue at Corinth, who was seized and beaten by the mob in the presence of Gallio, the Roman governor, when he refused to proceed against Paul at the instigation of the Jews (Acts 18:12-17).","verses":2,"father":"","mother":"","v":[1]},{"id":"chloe_943","name":"Chloe","also":"","summary":"Verdure, a female Christian (1 Cor. 1:11), some of whose household had informed Paul of the divided state of the Corinthian church.","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[11]},{"id":"peter_2745","name":"Simon","also":"Cephas, Simeon","summary":"Originally called Simon (=Simeon, i.e., “hearing”), a very common Jewish name in the New Testament. He was the son of Jona (Matt. 16:17). His mother is nowhere named in Scripture.","verses":175,"father":"Jonas","mother":"","v":[12]},{"id":"apollos_276","name":"Apollos","also":"","summary":"A Jew “born at Alexandria,” a man well versed in the Scriptures and eloquent (Acts 18:24; R.V., “learned”). He came to Ephesus (about A.D. 49), where he spake “boldly” in the synagogue (18:26), although he did not know as yet that Jesus of Nazareth was the Messiah.","verses":10,"father":"","mother":"","v":[12]},{"id":"crispus_961","name":"Crispus","also":"","summary":"Curled, the chief of the synagogue at Corinth (Acts 18:8).","verses":2,"father":"","mother":"","v":[14]},{"id":"gaius_1271","name":"Gaius","also":"","summary":"A Macedonian, Paul’s fellow-traveller, and his host at Corinth when he wrote his Epistle to the Romans (16:23). He with his household were baptized by Paul (1 Cor. 1:14).","verses":2,"father":"","mother":"","v":[14]},{"id":"stephanas_2801","name":"Stephanas","also":"","summary":"Crown, a member of the church at Corinth, whose family were among those the apostle had baptized (1 Cor. 1:16; 16:15, 17). He has been supposed by some to have been the “jailer of Philippi” (comp. Acts 16:33).","verses":3,"father":"","mother":"","v":[16]}],"places":[{"id":"corinth_306","name":"Corinth","kind":"City","lat":37.90604,"lon":22.87872,"summary":"A Grecian city, on the isthmus which joins the Peloponnesus to the mainland of Greece. It is about 48 miles west of Athens. The ancient city was destroyed by the Romans (B.C. 146), and that mentioned in the New Testament was quite a new city, having been rebuilt about a century afterwards and peopled by a colony of freedmen from Rome.","verses":6,"v":[2]}],"events":[],"traditions":[["baptism-who",16,16]],"sources":["Barnes","JFB","MHCC","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[3972,2822,2822,2822,652,652,5547,5547,2424,1223,2307,2307,2316,2316,2532,3588,80,4988],[3588,3588,1577,2316,2316,1722,2882,37,37,37,1722,5547,2424,2822,2822,40,40,40,4862,4862,3956,3588,5117,1941,1941,1941,3588,3686,1473,1473,2962,2424,5547,846,846,2532,1473],[5485,2532,1515,4771,4771,575,2316,1473,3962,2532,2962,2962,2424,5547],[2168,2168,2168,1473,2316,4012,4771,1909,1909,3588,5485,2316,1325,1325,4771,1722,5547,2424],[3754,1722,846,4148,4148,4148,4148,1722,3956,3956,1722,3956,3056,2532,3956,1108],[2531,3588,3142,3588,5547,950,950,1722,4771],[5620,4771,5302,5302,5302,3367,5486,5486,553,553,553,553,3588,602,1473,1473,2962,2424,5547],[3739,950,950,4771,2193,5056,5056,410,410,410,410,410,410,1722,3588,2250,1473,1473,2962,2424,5547],[2316,3739,2564,2564,2564,1519,2842,846,846,5207,2424,5547,1473,2962,4103,4103],[3870,3870,4771,4771,80,1223,3588,3686,1473,1473,2962,2424,5547,2443,3956,3956,3004,3004,3004,2532,2532,1510,1510,1510,3361,4978,1722,4771,1161,1161,1510,1510,1510,2675,1722,3563,2532,1106],[1473,80,3588,5514,5514,5514,1213,1213,1473,3754,1510,1510,2054,1722,4771],[3004,3004,3004,3778